This Python function uses a breadth-first search approach to simulate the rotting process. It initializes a queue with all the positions of initially rotten oranges and counts the number of fresh oranges. Then, it iteratively processes each level of the BFS, marking adjacent fresh oranges as rotten and reducing the count of fresh oranges. The time complexity is O(n*m), where n is the number of rows and m is the number of columns in the grid. The space complexity is also O(n*m) due to the use of the queue.
